   {id:'nerves',question:"Do players get nervous in finals?",answer:"Almost everyone does. Many players use a simple first action, like an easy pass, to settle their nerves.",followUp:{question:"What can I do before a big game?",answer:"Breathe out slowly, picture your first touch, and remind yourself of one job you are great at."}},
   {id:'extra-time',question:"How long is extra time?",answer:"In 11-a-side football it is usually two halves of 15 minutes. Tired legs make it a test of fitness and calm thinking.",followUp:{question:"What if it is still level after that?",answer:"Then many cup games go to a penalty shoot-out. Each team takes five kicks, and if it is still tied they keep going one kick each."}},
   {id:'neutral',question:"Why are some finals at a neutral stadium?",answer:"So neither team gets a home crowd. Both sets of fans share the stadium, which feels fair.",followUp:{question:"Do the fans sit apart?",answer:"Usually each team's fans get their own end, so both can sing for their side."}},
   {id:'trophy',question:"Who lifts the trophy first?",answer:"Usually the captain, after the whole team collects medals. Some captains share the lift with a teammate who worked extra hard.",followUp:{question:"Does the losing team get medals?",answer:"Often they get runners-up medals. Reaching a final is a big achievement too."}},
   {id:'cramp',question:"Why do players lie down in extra time?",answer:"Long games can cause cramp, a sudden tight muscle. Teammates and physios help stretch it out gently.",followUp:{question:"How do players avoid cramp?",answer:"Drinking water, eating well and good fitness all help. Gentle stretching in the breaks can too."}},
   {id:'halftime-plan',question:"Do coaches change plans at halftime of a final?",answer:"Very often. A coach might add a fresh runner, change the shape, or ask the team to press higher."},
   {id:'penalty-order',question:"Who decides who takes the penalties?",answer:"The coach usually picks the order after talking with players who feel confident. Calm takers often go first and last.",followUp:{question:"Why is the fifth kick special?",answer:"It can be the one that wins or saves the shoot-out, so coaches choose someone very steady."}},
   {id:'score-first',question:"Does scoring first win finals?",answer:"It helps, but it is not a promise. The team behind often attacks harder and the game can change fast."}
